---
import { withBase } from '../../lib/base';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DialogueRunner from '../../components/DialogueRunner.astro';
import scene from '../../data/dialogue-drive.json';
---
<BaseLayout title="The Drive — STATIC">
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
      <a href={withBase('/game#interactive-dialogue')} class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-dim transition-colors hover:text-violet-bright">&larr; back to STATIC</a>
      <p class="eyebrow mt-5 mb-3">CH 02 · Playable scene</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-5xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-tight text-ink md:text-6xl">{scene.meta.title}</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-dim">
        Two main characters, Ian and Saoirse, talk in the car after Ian picks her up
        on the road following her accident. They have not seen each other in ten years.
        The atmosphere in the car is awkward and tense. You are in control of the conversation.
        Your choices set flags that change later lines and gate later
        options. Four endings in all. Click to advance; click again to skip the type-on.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  
<section class="px-6 pb-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
      <DialogueRunner scene={scene} />
    <p class="mt-8 text-ink-dim">
        <strong class="text-ink">Design note:</strong> This scene runs on the game's dialogue
        system: persistent flags, gated choices, escalating reactions, and a hidden ending
        that rewards restraint. Choices made in the opening beats change what Ian and Saoirse say. 
        Narration beats pace the scene between
        lines, the way they would in the full game, where what you say in the car follows
        you for the rest of the investigation.
     </p>
     <p class="mt-8 text-ink-dim">   
        This scene also exists as a <a href={withBase('/game#screenplay-scene')} class="text-violet-bright underline">linear
        screenplay</a> — the canonical cut, as it happens in the novel, with margin notes on
        where the two versions diverge.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
